# Code owners for the harness paths. Design: ADR-ea8c, section 4, and ADR-ebe6.
# The main ruleset requires code-owner review (infra/github/ruleset.tf), so a PR that
# touches any path below needs an approval from @islomar. A GitHub App cannot be a code
# owner. There is no `*` line: other paths need only the ruleset's normal approval.
#
# Syntax: the last matching pattern wins. A pattern ending in `/` matches the directory
# and everything below it. A leading `/` anchors the pattern at the repository root.
# A pattern without `/` matches that file name in any directory. `!` and `[ ]` do not work.

# Harness: files that steer the agents, CI, infrastructure and this file.
/.github/          @islomar
/.claude/          @islomar
/factory/          @islomar
/infra/            @islomar
/scripts/          @islomar
/Makefile          @islomar
/CLAUDE.md         @islomar
/docs/decisions/   @islomar
/docs/knowledge/   @islomar

# Supply chain. Manifests, lockfiles, images and runtime pins have no code owner: the
# required check `supply-chain` takes the owner's place (ADR-ebe6). It passes for
# Dependabot-only PRs and otherwise needs the owner's approval on the head commit.
# The check itself and `.npmrc` (release-age settings and exemptions) stay owned.
# Keep the check's own lines even if the directory lines above are narrowed later.
.npmrc                               @islomar
/.github/workflows/supply-chain.yml  @islomar
/scripts/check_supply_chain.py       @islomar
/scripts/rerun_failed_supply_chain.py @islomar
